From: Paul-Louis Charriere <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: remove hardware flows before unbinding

Backport the 2026-10-26 pre-unbind cleanup proposal to Linux6.18.59.
Keep the existing BIND/UNBIND/error/netdev lifecycle and drain pending
hardware work before its callbacks are removed. The second GC handles
flows skipped while offload work was pending or GC preceded teardown.

This is the proposed pre-unbind fix, not the later hook-release rewrite.
It does not establish the cause of W1700K MLO throughput stalls.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/netfilter-devel/20261026035651.40052-1-plcharriere@gmail.com/
Fixes: 13210fc63f35 ("netfilter: nf_tables: imbalance in flowtable binding")
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charriere <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1273,6 +1273,19 @@
 	if (!nf_flowtable_hw_offload(flowtable))
 		return nf_flow_offload_xdp_setup(flowtable, dev, cmd);
 
+	/* Hardware rules are deleted through the block callbacks, so delete
+	 * the rules of this device's flows before unbinding it.  Run the GC
+	 * twice: the first run may skip flows with pending offload work, or
+	 * have started before the teardown.
+	 */
+	if (cmd == FLOW_BLOCK_UNBIND) {
+		nf_flow_table_gc_cleanup(flowtable, dev);
+		mod_delayed_work(system_power_efficient_wq,
+				 &flowtable->gc_work, 0);
+		flush_delayed_work(&flowtable->gc_work);
+		flush_workqueue(nf_flow_offload_del_wq);
+	}
+
 	if (dev->netdev_ops->ndo_setup_tc)
 		err = nf_flow_table_offload_cmd(&bo, flowtable, dev, cmd,
 						&extack);
